SonoForge release signing keys
==============================

The release workflow (.github/workflows/release.yml) publishes a detached GPG signature
`SHA256SUMS.asc` next to the checksum manifest of every release, signed by the subkey
below. What each guarantee covers is documented in docs/security/code-signing.md.

Primary key — kept offline, never used to sign releases:

    E231CA97068B6FD9DBA2696B56A26E00755AA57A    RSA 3072 [SC], expires 2028-11-22

Signing subkey — the only secret key material in CI (exported alone; the primary key
never leaves offline storage):

    1A5627BF368987B7F1DCC9409EE80D1A063BE8C8    RSA 3072 [S],  expires 2027-11-24

Verify a download:

    gpg --recv-keys E231CA97068B6FD9DBA2696B56A26E00755AA57A    # once, from keyserver.ubuntu.com
    gpg --verify SHA256SUMS.asc SHA256SUMS
    sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS --ignore-missing

The signature must verify against the fingerprints above (gpg prints the signing key's
fingerprint; `--status-fd 1` shows it as VALIDSIG). If a signature verifies under any
other key, or the manifest does not match the downloaded file, do not trust the download
and report it. Pin this file or the fingerprints out of band before relying on them:
a fingerprint published only next to the signature it validates proves nothing.

